.\" javaall(1) — comprehensive all-in-one man page for javars.
.\" Modeled after zshall(1): every section of the reference in one document.
.\" Render with:  man -l man/man1/javaall.1
.\" Install:      cp man/man1/javaall.1 /usr/local/share/man/man1/
.TH JAVAALL 1 "2026-10-03" "javars 0.1.13" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
javaall \- the javars comprehensive reference (invocation, language subset,
architecture, bytecode VM + Cranelift JIT, LSP, DAP)
.SH OVERVIEW
This is the all\-in\-one
.B javars
manual, modeled on
.BR zshall (1).
It concatenates the major sections of the javars reference into a single page so
you can grep with `/`:
.RS 2
.PP
.B 1.  INVOCATION
.RB "\(em " "flags, files, exit status"
.br
.B 2.  LANGUAGE SUBSET
.RB "\(em " "the supported Java subset"
.br
.B 3.  ARCHITECTURE
.RB "\(em " "lex \[->] parse \[->] lower \[->] fusevm VM + JIT"
.br
.B 4.  TOOLING
.RB "\(em " "\-\-lsp language server, \-\-dap debugger, dumps"
.br
.B 5.  DIAGNOSTICS
.RB "\(em " "error format and common messages"
.RE
.SH 1. INVOCATION
.B java
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIFILE.java\fR runs the
.B main
of the entry class in
.IR FILE.java .
The introspection flags
.RB ( \-\-dump\-tokens ", " \-\-dump\-ast ", " \-\-disasm )
print an artifact and exit without running;
.B \-\-tiers
runs the program and then reports the fusevm tier each chunk reached.
.B \-\-lsp
and
.B \-\-dap
speak their protocols over stdio and take no file.
See
.BR java (1)
for the per\-flag table.
.SH 2. LANGUAGE SUBSET
A compilation unit holds a
.B public static void main(String[] args)
entry point; every other member (static and instance methods, fields,
constructors, nested types) is compiled as well. See the README and
.I BUGS.md
in the source tree for the detailed feature list and known gaps.
.SS Declarations
Classes with single inheritance
.RB ( extends ),
interfaces (abstract and
.B default
methods), abstract classes,
.BR enum " types (including constructor arguments and per\-constant bodies),"
.B record
types, type\-erased generics, method overloading, and
.B static
fields and
.B static { }
blocks.
.SS Statements
Local declarations (including
.BR var ),
plain and compound assignment,
.BR if / else ,
.BR while ,
C\-style and enhanced
.BR for ,
classic and arrow
.BR switch ,
.BR break ,
.BR continue ,
.BR return ,
.BR throw ,
.BR try / catch / finally
(including try\-with\-resources), and
.BR System.out.print [ln]
calls.
.SS Expressions
Integer, floating, boolean, string, and char literals; arithmetic, comparison,
bitwise, shift, and short\-circuit logical operators; casts; lambdas and
method references; array creation and indexing; object creation, field access,
and method calls. Java's
.B +
concatenates when either operand is a
.BR String ;
an
.B int
operation wraps at 32 bits and whole
.B double
values print with a trailing
.B .0
to match
.BR java .
.SS Library
A modeled subset of the Java standard library:
.BR String ,
.BR StringBuilder ,
boxed wrappers,
.BR Arrays ,
.BR Collections ,
.B java.util
collections,
.BR java.util.regex ,
and
.BR String.format / printf .
An unsupported construct is a parse or compile error rather than a silent
mis\-run.
.SH 3. ARCHITECTURE
.EX
Java source \[->] lexer \[->] parser (AST) \[->] lower to fusevm bytecode \[->] fusevm VM + Cranelift JIT
.EE
.PP
There is no local
.I vm.rs
or
.IR jit.rs .
Arithmetic and comparisons lower to native fusevm ops so the tracing JIT can
compile hot loops; Java\-specific behaviour (the
.B String
.B +
overload, Java\-flavoured value formatting) is supplied by the host numeric hook
and the print builtins. The same fusevm engine hosts zshrs, stryke, awkrs, elisp,
and ruby, so JIT and VM improvements benefit all of them at once.
.SH 4. TOOLING
.SS Language server (\-\-lsp)
.B java \-\-lsp
speaks LSP over stdio: completion and hover from the language\-reference corpus in
.IR src/reference.rs
\(em every keyword, operator, type, library method, throwable, functional
interface, class member, format conversion and runtime builtin the build
implements, each with a signature, a description and an example (the same table
that generates
.IR docs/reference.html ),
and diagnostics from the runtime's own parser \(em a syntax error maps to a
diagnostic on the reported line. It is read\-only; no output reaches the terminal.
.SS Debugger (\-\-dap)
.B java \-\-dap
speaks the Debug Adapter Protocol over stdio. The program is compiled with
per\-statement line markers (only in this mode) and run on the pure interpreter so
the markers always fire. Supported: line breakpoints, single\-stepping
.RB ( next / stepIn / stepOut ,
which all advance to the next statement in the single
.B main
frame), a
.B stackTrace
of the current frame, and
.B variables
inspection of
.BR main 's
locals. Program output
.RB ( System.out )
is captured and forwarded as
.B output
events so it never corrupts the protocol channel.
.SS Dumps
.B \-\-dump\-tokens
prints the token stream,
.B \-\-dump\-ast
the parsed AST, and
.B \-\-disasm
a fusevm bytecode disassembly \(em each then exits.
.PP
.B \-\-tiers
runs the program, then reports which fusevm execution tier took each chunk.
.SH 5. DIAGNOSTICS
Errors are written to standard error in the form
.IR "javars: <reason>" ,
for example an unterminated string literal or an unexpected token.
The process exits 1 on a lex/parse/compile error, an unreadable file, or a
missing file argument, and 0 on success. An uncaught Java exception is reported
and exits non\-zero;
.B System.exit(n)
exits with \fIn\fR modulo 256.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR java (1)
The focused invocation page. Source and issue tracker:
https://github.com/MenkeTechnologies/javars
.SH AUTHOR
Part of the fusevm language family.
